- a concrete model slug—never `openrouter/auto` and never a `~latest` alias;
- `allow_fallbacks: false`, a recorded provider preference/order, and `require_parameters: true`;
- fixed `reasoning_effort: high`, temperature, tool settings, timeout, and retry policy;
- request model slug plus resolved model/provider/router metadata, token usage, cost estimate, and adapter commit;
- independent attempts rather than a shared seed claim when the model does not support seeds.

- task IDs, licenses, source/task manifests, and hashes;
- role prompts, output schemas, workflow version, and declared revision cap;
- arm materializer version, expected visible-token budgets, and Proofpress verifier version;
- OpenRouter model/provider settings, effort, temperature, retry/timeout policy, and pricing snapshot;
- scorer version, blind-audit rubric, randomization/attempt order, and stop conditions.
